1 GENERAL Military use only.
Due to parking limitation, full stop landing is strictly PPR (24 HR ) for non-home-based aircraft and helicopters. Contact Wing OPS via AFS or by phone (see EBFS AD 2.2 ). The PPR number shall be inserted in the flight plan under item 18.
2 TAXI REGULATIONS NIL
3 APRON REGULATIONS NIL
4 RUNWAY REGULATIONS Operational limitations for flights on secondary RWY (08R/26L):
General: Only home base ACFT may perform take-off and landing on the secondary RWY while the primary RWY is open. Nevertheless, TWR may authorize take-off and landing on the secondary RWY for other ACFT if the situation dictates (traffic load, QRA scramble in progress, etc.);
Qualification needs to be obtained prior landing (pilots must be aware of the secondary RWY characteristics and all obstacles in the vicinity, furthermore pilots have to perform a practice low approach and a touch-and-go landing prior full stop landing;
Take-off and landing: Single take-off and landing will be of application;
No simultaneous approaches will be conducted on both RWY at the same time;
Slow lane will not be of application;
Separation between two landing ACFT is one RWY length;
Out of SFO pattern only practice low approach authorized;
No precision approach available (neither ILS nor PAR );
No night OPS will occur except for QRA A-scramble take-off when primary RWY is closed;
Training approaches: For home base ACFT , training approaches are authorized to gain or maintain qualification;
For non-home base ACFT , 01 training approach will be authorized. According traffic, ATC may authorize more approaches;
RMK : For fast jets, only practice low approach authorized (no touch-and-go landing).
5 SPECIFIC TRAFFIC REGULATIONS NIL
